  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PAGoDA with CDB for the Road Maintenance and Management System in St Vincent and Grenadines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to enhance the quality of life of the citizens of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines and to improve climate change resilience of the road network in particular rural roads. This will contribute to the stimulation of economic activities in rural communities and reduced vulnerability to climate change. The specific objectives of the intervention will be to (a) strengthen the national road management and maintenance programme whilst minimising environmental impacts and (b) upgrade and &apos;&apos;climate-proof&apos;&apos; village and feeder roads.According to the Action Document, for each of the specific objectives the main expected results are: a.Strengthen the Road Management and Maintenance Programme (i) Road and traffic legislations revised; (ii) Road strategy plan for Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, including:a)environmental methods for rehabilitation (safeguards) b)climate proofing measures (resilient roads) developed(iii) Road network base map updated based on the World Bank GIS Mapping; (iv) Current Road Maintenance Management System (RMMS), including the development of affordable and acceptable maintenance standards  developed and strengthened; and (v) Institutional strengthening/capacity building implementedb.Upgrade and &apos;&apos;climate-proof&apos;&apos; village and feeder roads The main result under this component is that the selected roads are rehabilitated. The RMMS will be tested as a pilot project through a selection of feeder and village roads to be upgraded and executed on a priority basis. The given indicative list of priority roads may change subject to outcomes of the RRMS tests, considering the following factors: (i) Complement of on-going programmes, such as the BAM and The Post Trough Emergency Infrastructure Rehabilitation Programme implemented by the World Bank (B Envelope); (ii) Improve accessibility to farming area; (iii) Improve accessibility to health and other social facilities; (iv) Provide alternative routes in the event of major disruptions to network such as landslides or/and coastal erosion; (v) Potential for employment generation during construction; (vi) Introduction of environmental safeguards and climate proofing parameters.</narrative>
  </description>
